MixRelay uses the Advanced Linux Sound Architecture library (libasound) on Linux.
The ALSA library and its use are covered by the GNU Lesser General Public License
version 2.1; the licence text is included in COPYING.

MixRelay dynamically links to the system's ALSA library. The distribution supplies
that library, its copyright notices and corresponding source code. An ABI-compatible
modified system library can be substituted. Modification for the customer's own use
and reverse engineering to debug such modifications are permitted as required by
section 6 of the LGPL.

Upstream source: https://github.com/alsa-project/alsa-lib
